7 + 10 = 17 In this problem, we are starting with 7 lollipops. Erin's mother gives her 10 more lollipops. Erin's total number of lollipops is 7 + 10 = 17. Then, Erin gives 3 lollipops to Ella. To find the number of lollipops Erin has left, we subtract the number of lollipops she gave to Ella (3) from her total number of lollipops (17). 17 - 3 = 14. Therefore, Erin has 14 lollipops left. \boxed{14}
7 + 10 = 17
17 - 3 = 14
\boxed{14}
